From 7c714773da463416c793678878faaae1e383e85e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bherbruck <brennen.herbruck@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:22:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(ui): a refusal on the status strip is drawn as an
 alert

When the status line carries a refusal - a command refused through the
feedback path, a dark cell's "cannot ..." note, or one of the shell's
refusal phrasings - the strip draws it in the error ink, bold, behind a
"!" marker on an error-tinted band, until the next status replaces it.
Ordinary status text stays dim.

Fixes #192

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 RECOMMENDED.md                         | 17 ++++++
 crates/ui/src/egui_app/mod.rs          |  1 +
 crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs        | 12 +++-
 crates/ui/src/egui_app/status_alert.rs | 76 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 crates/ui/src/egui_app/status_alert.rs

